+/*
+ * MM21 to NV12 on the GPU, the way ChromeOS's Chrome detiles MediaTek decoder
+ * output (MT8189 has no MDP3 path for it). The decoder's CAPTURE planes are
+ * imported as linear RGBA8 images (4 bytes per texel) and a fragment shader
+ * gathers each output texel from its tile: MM21 stores 16-byte-wide tiles,
+ * 32 rows tall for luma and 16 for the interleaved chroma, each tile one
+ * contiguous block, a row of tiles taking stride * tile_height bytes. The
+ * NV12 surface's two planes are the render targets.
+ *
+ * Only with Mesa (Panfrost): EGL is loaded privately (RTLD_LOCAL) and every
+ * entry point resolved through eglGetProcAddress, so nothing clashes with the
+ * ANGLE copy of libGLESv2 that Chrome loads in the same process.
+ * V4L2R_GL_DETILE=0 turns it off; any failure falls back to the CPU path.
+ */
